<WI>-<slug>.md` and commit with nothing else staged. Verify with\n`verdict.governing_rev(root, \"HEAD\")` — it should still peel back to the close\ncommit, proving the record-only commits did not buy the lane another round.\nCorollary the same asymmetry creates: those paths are excluded from the\nidentity but **not** from the checks, so a green taken before your own log/\ntelemetry commits does not cover them — re-drive at the actual tip.\n\nAlso: the full suite must run on a worktree with `docs/stage` regenerated\n(`derive_stage.py --root .`), since a spine-touching branch moves `drafted` and\na lane must not commit that trunk-owned generated artifact. Related:\n[[worker-lane-close-ritual-traps]], [[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
