{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegEbZe3foW2PhaYLamGv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-579 is closed and the round-025 rework is discharged on evidence I drove myself.\n\n**The three findings, re-derived rather than read.** Sessions 026/027 had already landed fixes, so the risk here was believing an inherited claim about a fix:\n\n- **IF-175 `Data`** — parsed from the TOML: 145 chars against the 160 ceiling; `trace.py --strict-integrity` reports `interface-findings=0`.\n- **LLR-207** — `detail`/`rationale` token-scanned for `round <n>`/`WI-`/`OI-`/`defect`/`finding`: clean. The one provenance FINDING left is LLR-197's `WI-448`, and it's inherited — `git diff 0ecc62b..HEAD` touches exactly two design rows (LLR-207, LLR-208).\n- **The unfiltered green** — re-taken, not carried. The earlier readings were at `4332a073` and `430a7fe8`; two commits had landed since. Those paths (`docs/log.d/`, `docs/iteration/`) are excluded from the verdict record's tree identity but *not* from the checks that read them, so the prior green didn't cover them.\n\n```\n3349 passed, 25 skipped in 626.95s (0:10:26)\n```\nat `957e0039`, on a worktree with the trunk-owned `docs/stage` regenerated. Commit bar green at both commits (smoke 1510 passed/8 skipped, 34.3 s; enforcer 48.6 s vs 60 s; `check_docs --stale` OK).\n\n**The `docs/stage` claim, driven by field diff:** `drafted` (9→13) and its fingerprint are the *only* two differing lines — `stage`, `stage-ord`, `stage-of`, `floored`, `settled-stage`, `live-stage`, `phase`, `per-phase`, `per-phase-live` are byte-identical. Caused by this branch, benign because a lane must not commit that generated artifact.\n\n**One thing worth flagging.** I drove this lane's own readers against this lane. `governing_rev(HEAD)` peels through all three record-only commits back to the close at `430a7fe8`, and the identity is unchanged after my two commits — so writing the evidence didn't stale the evidence. But `round_entries` at that identity is **empty** and `phases_owed` returns `['REVIEW-A']`: the rework changed the non-record tree, so the round-025 verdict stopped governing the moment it was answered. Seven logged rounds sit on this branch and none speaks for this tree. **The lane owes a fresh REVIEW-A before it can merge** — that's the gate refusing to let its own author close over it, not a defect.\n\nBoth commits carry the `WI: WI-579` trailer; spec is in `docs/archive/work/complete/` with `specref` cleared and Deliverable before Context; the stale empty `active/` dir and the scratch worktree are cleaned up. Working tree clean, nothing pushed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":111327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":415},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6a44a33-b6fa-4301-8a9d-8a491e68bd04","uuid":"435a7450-ce89-4864-8a69-8fab5031f849","request_id":"req_011CegEbYFTjSM5En8AHvMom"}
